ok\nStaff Handbook\nCampus Services\nFacilities Management\nOffice of Research\nMail Services\nPrinting\nPantherDining & Catering\nParking & Transportation\nPantherCard MOBILE\nTravel Reservations\nPR & Marketing Communications\nLegal Services\nInstitutional Effectiveness\nEmeriti Association\nTechnology\nEmail\nSend A File\nDigital Measures\nPAWS\nGoSOLAR\niCollege\nOneUSG Connect\nPanthermart\nSpectrum (requires VPN)\nAsset Works\nTraining and Learning\nCETLOE\nStacks for State\n\u00d7\nUseful Links\nDirectory (Login Required)\nStaff A-Z Index\nNews & Updates\nAcademic Calendar\nLibrary\nHelp Center\nSafety & Security\nFacilities\nEthics Hotline\nIdentity & Comms. ToolKit\nCollege to Career\nGet The LiveSafe App\nSkip to content\nSkip to primary nav\nMathematics and Statistics\nCollege of Arts & Sciences\nMain navigation\nAbout\nDepartment Contacts\nFaculty & Staff Directory\nNews & Events\nEmployment Opportunities\nAcademics\nUndergraduate\nB.S. Mathematics\n5-year Bachelor\u2019s/Masters Programs (Dual Degree)\nGraduate\nM.S. Mathematics\nM.S. Applied Statistics\nPh.D. Mathematics and Statistics\nResearch\nGiving\nFinancial Support\nFinancial Support\nStudents\nUndergraduate Students\nUndergraduate Advising Information\nUndergraduate Registration Support\nUndergrad Courses\nAll Courses\nCatalog: Mathematics Courses\nCourse Content\nCourse Syllabus\nGraduate Students\nCurrent Students\nGraduate Registration Guildeline\nGraduate Advising Information\nFinancial Support\nGraduate Courses\nAll Courses\nCatalog: Mathematics Courses\nCatalog: Math Education Courses\nCatalog: Statistics Courses\nStudent Activities\nMath and Statistics Club\nAMS Graduate Student Chapter\nSIAM Student Chapter\nUndergraduate Research\nStudent Learning Labs\nMathematics Interactive Learning Environment (MILE)\nSTEM\nResources & Forms\nUndergraduate Forms and Policies\nGraduate Forms and Policies\nGraduate Student Resources\nFINANCIAL SUPPORT\nMath & Stat Graduate Assistantships\nTypes of Assistantship\nThe Department of Mathematics and Statistics offers several types of graduate assistantships for M.S. and Ph.D. students.\nGraduate students can apply for\nGraduate Lab Assistantship (GLA)\nGraduate Teaching Assistantship (GTA)\nGraduate Research Assistantship (GRA)\nPh.D. students can also apply for\nBrains and Behavior (B&B) Fellowship\nMolecular Basis of Disease (MBD) Fellowship\nUniversity 2CI Doctoral Fellowship\nApplication Deadline\nSee the graduate admission page and the application deadlines for the Master of Science degree program and the Ph.D. Mathematics and Statistics program.\nTerms of Assistantship\nA Ph.D. student can have a maximum of 3 or 5 years of support as a Ph.D. graduate assistant. The precise limit depends on the credit hours transferred to the program. A student transferring the equivalent of an M.S. (24 hours) will be limited to 3 years of support. A student transferring no credit will be eligible for 5 years support.\nThe B&B and the MBD Fellowships are limited to a maximum of 3 years.\nAn M.S. student can have a maximum of two years as a graduate assistant.\nTo become a GTA, it is necessary to have completed 18 hours of graduate level courses in Math/Stat and to have taken Math 9116 (Teaching College Mathematics). Prospective international student GTAs are also required to take ESL 7500 (Teaching at the University for International Teaching Assistants).\nRate of Pay\nThe department offers several types of graduate assistantships on a competitive basis to the students in our graduate programs. The vast majority of our Ph.D. students are fully supported by these assistantships, as well as a large percentage of the MS students. For specific information, please contact the graduate directors.\nTuition Waiver\nCollege of Arts and Sciences has a minimum enrollment level for students receiving a tuition waiver:\nFall/Spring\nSummer\nPh.D. student\n12 hours\n9 hours\nM.S. student\n12 hours\n9 hours\nStudents should contact the appropriate graduate director to be assigned to courses to make up any additional needed hours.\nContact Us\nDepartment of Mathematics and Statistics\n404-413-6400\nDEPARTMENT CONTACTS\nFACULTY & STAFF DIRECTORY\nOffice/Delivery Address\nDepartment of Mathematics and Statistics\nGeorgia State University\n25 Park Place, 14th Floor\nAtlanta, Georgia 30303-3083, USA\nFind Us on the Map\nUSPS Mailing Address:\nDepartment of Mathematics and Statistics\nGeorgia State University\nP.O. Box 4110\nAtlanta, GA 30302-4110\nSocial Media\nAbout\nContact Georgia State\nEmployment\nUniversity Policies\nOffice of the President\nCampus Maps\nAdministration\nNews & Events\nStudent Success\nAdmissions\nDegrees & Majors\nGraduate Programs\nCollege to Career\nUniversity Library\nLaw Library\nBookstore\nConnections\nMagazine\nAlumni\nGiving\nArts & Ideas\nRialto Center\nAlbum 88 (WRAS-FM)\nResearch\nOffice of Research\nAthletics\nTickets\nSports\nPanther Athletic Club\nRecruits\nNews\nCampus Life\nStudent Engagement\nCounseling Center\nHealth Center\nHousing\nParking\nDining\nRecreation\nSafety\nGeorgia State University100 Auburn Ave NE Atlanta, GA 30303404-413-2000\nContact Georgia StateView Legal Statement & Human Trafficking NoticePrivacy NoticesState AuthorizationEthics HotlineWebsite Feedback\u00a92026 Georgia State University\nFacebook\nTwitter\nLinkedIn\nEmail\nSend this to a friend\nYour emailRecipient email\nSendCancel", "links": [["Alumni", "https://alumni.gsu.edu"], ["Faculty & Staff", "javascript:void(0);"], ["Students", "javascript:void(0);"], ["Undergraduate Advising Information", "https://mathstat.gsu.edu/undergraduate-advising-information/"], ["Undergraduate Registration Support", "https://mathstat.gsu.edu/undergraduate-registration-support/"], ["All Courses", "https://mathstat.gsu.edu/undergraduate-courses/"], ["Catalog: Mathematics Courses", "https://catalog.gsu.edu/undergraduate20202021/subject/math/"], ["Course Content", "https://mathstat.gsu.edu/document/course-content/?wp